hypotheses.statement:
For every $p\in(0,1)$, there is an open $1$-periodic set $H\subseteq\mathbb R$ with $\rho(H)\le6p$ such that $$\label{eq:periodic-hitting}
 \text{for every }x\in\mathbb R\text{ and }t\in[1,2],
 \quad x+tq^n\in H\text{ for some integer }n\ge1.$$

evidence.quote:
